*======================================================================
* keys.a99 - keyboard matrix scan via the TMS9901
*
* KSCAN reads all six keyboard columns into KEYMAP (one byte each,
* 0 bit = pressed).  KEYGET translates the first pressed key to ASCII
* with edge detection so a held key reports once.
* Matrix: column select on CRU bits 18-20, rows read on bits 3-10.
*======================================================================

* KSCAN - fill KEYMAP.  Uses R1-R4, R12.  Leaf.
KSCAN  LI   R2,KEYMAP          6 output bytes, one per column
       CLR  R1                 column number in the high byte
       LI   R3,6               six keyboard columns
KSC1   LI   R12,>0024          CRU bits 18-20 select the column
       LDCR R1,3               3 bits from the high byte of R1
       NOP                     settle time for the 9901 outputs
       NOP
       LI   R12,>0006          CRU bits 3-10 are the row lines
       CLR  R4                 STCR of 8 bits leaves the low byte alone
       STCR R4,8               row bits -> high byte, bit 3 -> LSB
       MOVB R4,*R2+            store: 0 bit = key down
       AI   R1,>0100           next column
       DEC  R3
       JNE  KSC1
       RT

* KEYGET - R0 = ASCII (high byte) of a newly pressed key, or 0.
* Uses R1-R5.  Leaf.
KEYGET LI   R1,KEYMAP          scan the columns in order
       LI   R2,KTAB            8 ASCII codes per column
       LI   R3,6
KG1    MOVB *R1+,R4            this column's row bits
       INV  R4                 now 1 = pressed
       ANDI R4,>FF00           high byte only (INV touched the low byte too)
       JNE  KG2                something pressed in this column
       AI   R2,8               next column's table row
       DEC  R3
       JNE  KG1
       CLR  R0                 nothing pressed: clear edge state
       MOVB R0,@KEYLST
       RT
KG2    SRL  R4,8               bit r of the low byte = row r
       CLR  R5                 row index
KG3    SRL  R4,1               shift bit 0 into carry
       JOC  KG4                carry set: this row is pressed
       INC  R5
       JMP  KG3
KG4    A    R5,R2              table entry for (column, row)
       CLR  R0                 (low byte clean: callers compare whole words)
       MOVB *R2,R0             ASCII, or 0 for modifiers
       CB   R0,@KEYLST
       JEQ  KG5                same key still held
       MOVB R0,@KEYLST
       RT
KG5    CLR  R0
       RT

* Key table: 6 columns x 8 rows.  0 = modifier / unused.
KTAB   BYTE '=',' ',13,0,0,0,0,0
       TEXT '.LO92SWX'
       TEXT ',KI83DEC'
       TEXT 'MJU74FRV'
       TEXT 'NHY65GTB'
       TEXT '/;P01AQZ'
       EVEN
